## Announced / upcoming

**Black Doldrums — Repetition Compulsion:** artist text states **13 November 2026**, with a preorder and three advance tracks. It explains that an October date was a Bandcamp preorder workaround; the opened current page now also displays November in its release field. Use the explicit November date, recheck before release, and exclude from released-album rankings at this cutoff. It is described as the third studio album, so the act is not a debut discovery. [Artist preorder page](https://blackdoldrums.bandcamp.com/album/repetition-compulsion).

**The Last Decade — Rebirth Of Suffering:** **20 November 2026** via Metalville Records. International gothic rock act described by the label as drawing roots from gothic and dark rock; the band's own term is "Endtimes rock". Debut album. Lineup combines members of The Mission, Nosferatu, End of Green, Love Like Blood, Seekers Are Lovers and Schwarzer Engel; introduced as a "gothic supergroup" at the 2024 Mystic Festival, Poland. Physical editions include a limited-to-333 vinyl and a deluxe digipak with a 16-page booklet. Established-act members, so "debut album" refers to the project, not new individual musicians. Label-store descriptions are promotional. [Metalville shop listing](https://metalville-shop.com/products/the-last-decade-rebirth-of-suffering-natural-black-smoke-lp-20-11-2026) gives 20.11.2026 and the 333-copy limit; [Season of Mist listing](https://shop.season-of-mist.com/products/the-last-decade-rebirth-of-suffering-cd-vinyl) confirms label and date.

**La Mano Sinistra — Omelas:** **6 November 2026** via Bat-Cave Productions. Debut album by a Bologna trio (formed 2025) — Davide Sacco vocals/lyrics, Gianluca Lo Presti bass/electronics, Giuseppe Lo Bue guitars/electronics. Recorded at Loto Studio, Ravenna. A darkwave concept album based on Ursula K. Le Guin's *The Ones Who Walk Away from Omelas*; the band name references *The Left Hand of Darkness*. Debut single "Unnecessary Perfection" went to streaming 2 October 2026. Description is post-punk/darkwave rather than core gothic rock. Two independent music-press sources agree on the date, but the Bat-Cave Bandcamp album page was not reachable at the check time (404), so the label page itself is unconfirmed. [ReGen Magazine, 8 October 2026](https://regenmag.com/news/news-italian-post-punk-trio-la-mano-sinistra-soon-to-release-debut-album-inspired-by-philosophical-work-by-ursula-k-le-guin/); [Terra Relicta, 8 October 2026](https://terrarelicta.com/publications/news/la-mano-sinistra-unveils-debut-single-and-video-unnecessary-perfection).

**Vampire Valentine — Scarred & Sacred:** **25 October 2026** via Morella Records. Six-track **EP**, so it stays out of the annual full-length ranking. Fourth Morella release since signing 15 January 2026, following their August self-titled debut album. Newcastle darkwave/post-punk trio; band cites The Sisters of Mercy, Twin Tribes, She Past Away and Lebanon Hanover. Three of the six tracks are instrumentals, including a "darksynth" cut and one built on 1980s horror soundtrack sound. [Side-Line, 2 October 2026](https://www.side-line.com/vampire-valentine-scarred-and-sacred/).

**David J — Postcards from the Afterlife:** **27 November 2026** on 51 Recordings, double LP/CD/digital. Fourteen songs from David J, Bauhaus and Love and Rockets co-founder. First single "Requiem for the Rose Garden" released 8 October 2026. J describes the material as soulful, hazy 1960s orchestral pop, European chanson and alternative rock, with a finale recorded with members of the Prague Symphony and Philharmonic orchestras — related-artist watchlist, not a core gothic rock release. [Side-Line, 8 October 2026](https://www.side-line.com/david-j-requiem-for-the-rose-garden/).

## Emerging discoveries

- **Kylmä Krypta:** eligible under an early-discography definition; the album mixes new material with re-recorded older songs. Hamburg-based act with Finnish lyrics, an unusual route into 80s post-punk.
- **La Mano Sinistra:** eligible under a debut-album definition. 2025 formation, so genuinely new; album-level fit still pending label-page confirmation.
- **Vioflesh:** eligible under an album-level discovery definition; discography history beyond 2026 not verified.
- **The Last Decade:** eligible under a debut-album definition, but composed of established scene members — a "gothic supergroup", not a new band of newcomers.
- **Mica:** eligible under a debut-album definition, with related styles labeled; formation date unverified.
- **Reflection Black:** eligible under an early-discography definition, based on the second-album claim and 2023 debut. "Rising" in the page is promotional wording, not independent proof of popularity.

These are research candidates, not a best-new-bands ranking. Seek independent appraisal and wider geographical coverage, including Chile/Latin America and Asian scenes. Keep EPs, singles, live releases, compilations, and reissues separate. Use the actual calendar year when continuing; current-year rankings are best so far with a stated cutoff.

